@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-credentials-are-native-and-confined
The native adapter MUST keep Pully sessions and optional Access credentials in this
app's non-synchronizing Keychain, accessible only while unlocked on this device.
Credential records MUST be bound to the normalized configured server and account,
MUST NOT be returned for another server, and MUST NOT enter URLs, defaults, logs or
analytics. Native code MUST NOT implement a second Pully RPC client. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision, the chosen plan's Authentication section,
and root phone-api-one-account and google-sign-in-same-account.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-account-reset-invalidates-observers
Sign-out, server changes and credential changes MUST synchronously invalidate the
active source before another source can be used. A late sign-in or verification
answer for an earlier source MUST NOT install credentials. A restored Keychain
session MUST require server verification before it becomes the active account.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS decision and chosen account/cache ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-google-uses-registered-native-client
Native Google sign-in MUST remain unavailable without a registered iOS client and
its reversed-client-ID callback scheme. It MUST request an ID token for the
existing server's web client ID, and MUST leave signature, audience, expiry and
email-allowlist validation to that server. It MUST NOT add GitHub OAuth or store a
Google client secret. Source: root google-sign-in-same-account and the chosen
21 Oct 2026 iOS plan's Authentication section.
